Dev task 06: a small INI-style configuration parser.
-- task.json --
{"id": "dev-06-config", "cluster": "dev", "created_at": null,
 "test_command": ["{python}", "-B", "-m", "unittest", "{hidden_modules}"],
 "timeout_s": 900, "grading_timeout_s": 120}
-- prompt.md --
Implement `parse_config(text)` in `conf/parse.py`. It returns a dict of sections, each a dict of string keys to string values.

- `[name]` starts a section; keys before any section go into the section `""` (the empty string), which appears in the result only if it has keys.
- `key = value` sets a key; spaces around the key and around the value are stripped. A value may contain `=`; only the first `=` separates.
- Lines whose first non-space character is `#` or `;` are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
- If a key repeats inside a section, the last value wins.
- Any other line raises `ValueError` whose message contains `line N`, N being the 1-based line number.

Do not use `configparser`.
-- start/conf/__init__.py --
